Have your technicians save this quick guide to their phones to verify operations during installations.
📋 Pre-Flight Bench ChecklistEnsure the CryptoJS source script code is successfully copied into a separate script tab inside the Google Apps Script editor. If this is missing, records will hit the gateway but fail to write into the spreadsheet rows.Populate the Config sheet tab with your target parameters before deploying hardware. The system will throw an error if an unmapped Node ID sends a payload.
📶 Field Installation StepsPower up the Central Gateway Hub first.Open the mobile configuration webpage on your phone. Connect to the hub via Bluetooth within the first 30 seconds to configure the localized Wi-Fi SSID, Password, and API Webhook or Google Script string ID.Mount your Sensor Nodes onto the upper surfaces of the fiberglass tank structures. Keep the 5dBi external whip antenna pointed vertically up toward the sky.Power up the Node. Connect your phone to it via the webpage within its 30-second boot window. Set its unique Node ID, Sleep Interval, and 16-character AES Key (ensuring this matches the entry value in Column Q of your Config sheet row).
🔍 Troubleshooting Real-Time Matrix LookupsSymptomProbable CauseCorrective Action Steps

Data fails to write to the spreadsheet, but the Hub's Serial log reads: "Connection to local instance failed."Incorrect Wi-Fi routing parameters or a typo in the destination Webhook URL.Power-cycle the Hub to open its 30-second Bluetooth portal. Re-enter the Wi-Fi credentials and ensure there are no trailing spaces or missing characters in your API Webhook string or Google ID.

The Hub's log flags "Decryption/Parsing failed: Error".Character length or value mismatch with your AES key.Double-check that the AES key typed into your mobile browser matches the string in Column Q of your Config sheet row exactly. Verify that both keys are exactly 16 characters long.

Values display correctly, but fields read constant "0 mV" or max "3300 mV".Electrical wiring issue or open circuit on your P-MOSFET tracking lines.Check the wire traces on your sensor terminal blocks. Ensure your P-MOSFET gate is switching correctly on IO19 and your analog probes are receiving steady supply currents during their 2-second wake cycles.

Nodes miss data entries consistently during rainy or overcast conditions.Severe signal degradation or echo distortions caused by low antenna heights.Ensure your tank whip antennas are mounted completely above the fluid lines. If needed, swap out the hub's 3dBi whip antenna for an exterior 5dBi fiberglass rod antenna mounted on a high roofline or external wall pole to improve your link budget.
